      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "United States president Donald Trump announces a 30% tariff increase on imported items from Mexico and the European Union to take effect on August 1. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Sports",
      "text": "In tennis, Iga Świątek defeats Amanda Anisimova in the women's singles final 6–0, 6–0 to win her first Wimbledon title, becoming the first Pole to do so. This is the third major final to have a double bagel scoreline and the first since 1988. ((The Independent)) ((WTA))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Arts and culture",
      "text": "UNESCO adds 26 landmarks to the UNESCO World Heritage list. ((UNESCO World Heritage Convention)) ((Newsweek))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Three people, including a baby, are killed and twenty people are hospitalized in an apartment fire in Ankara, Turkey. ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "Representatives of New Caledonia sign an accord with the French government to become the \"State of New Caledonia\" within the French Republic, subject to a referendum. The new state would immediately gain control of some foreign affairs, and would have the option of gaining further powers, subject to further referenda. ((Al Jazeera)) ((The New York Times))"
    },
    {
